[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue with one fix queued. Read report by report, it holds
three problems. Each needs its own fix, and each now has its own ticket.

<Callout kind="warn">
The parser fix queued for #4471 does not close #4471. The booking-v3 form and the one-day moves
stay broken after it ships.
</Callout>

## What is in #4471

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

The table is built from the ticket export at render time, so the counts follow the desk as it
keeps merging. Every report counts once, under one problem.

## How to tell them apart

- **`parser`**: the shared parser reads every date month first, and every tenant on file writes
  the day first. The day and the month swap: 2 March becomes 3 February. It reaches every channel
  of every tenant.
- **`hint`**: the booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field, but reads what people
  type the tenant's way, day first. People follow the hint, and the date swaps. Only reports that
  came in through the form, at a tenant on booking-v3. Fixing the parser does not fix this; the
  hint has to match what the form reads.
- **`one-day`**: the booking moves by one day, not by a swap. Tuesday becomes Monday, one client
  gets Tuesday while another in a different time zone gets Monday, an invite arrives before the
  booking was made. That looks like a time zone shift when the date is stored or sent, not a
  parser bug. The desk had already listed these reports as one-day moves in its notes, but
  [#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) still counts them under the parser.

## Why one ticket hid three

- Triage merges on the subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)).
  "Wrong date" fits all three problems, so all three landed in one ticket. Merging on subject
  alone needs a cause check before it.
- The intake tag is a guess from the reporter's browser, not from the tenant. The table shows
  how often it was right. Group by tenant, form and channel, as `causes.ts` does, not by tag.
- The cause table on [#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) already marked `hint` as "no ticket of its own"
  and footnoted the one-day moves. Status `known` made it read as finished.

